Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: reset the device on panic without waking MHI

The panic notifier resets the device with the same register helpers as
normal operation. While ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_INIT_DONE is set, every access
beyond ACCESS_ALWAYS_OFF first calls the WCN7850 wakeup op, which is
mhi_device_get_sync(). That sleeps until the MHI state machine reports M0,
and the state machine runs in interrupts and workers that cannot run once
panic() has stopped the other CPUs. The panicking task sleeps in the
notifier, so panic() never reaches kmsg_dump() or the panic reboot and the
phone stays frozen until the buttons reset it.

Clear INIT_DONE before the reset, as ath12k_pci_power_down() does before
the same sw_reset. The accesses then skip both the wakeup and the matching
release, and the reset becomes a best effort that cannot block.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
@@ -1475,7 +1475,15 @@
 
 static int ath12k_pci_panic_handler(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 {
+	struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci = ath12k_pci_priv(ab);
+
+	/* The MHI wakeup used by register access sleeps until the device
+	 * reaches M0, which cannot happen once panic() has stopped the
+	 * other CPUs. Reset without it, as power down does.
+	 */
+	clear_bit(ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_INIT_DONE, &ab_pci->flags);
+
 	ath12k_pci_sw_reset(ab, false);
 
 	return NOTIFY_OK;
 }
